 Attempt2 is also preserved, with its exact source/approval under `pre-issue-refusal/`. It cleanly stopped after205.931 seconds at the ordinary-Issue refusal assertion, after public audit proved two accepted rewards, zero births and one reserved signed batch. Its error code was not recorded. Independent source inspection proves the existing Issue handler maps every underlying non-Busy error, including capacity, to `outcome_unknown`; this successor respects that conservative boundary and proves no new job only after joined physical audit.
+
+Attempt3 is preserved with exact source/approval under `pre-wall-expiry/`: it passed phase05 then cleanly failed the post-sleep wall-expiry assertion at523.821 seconds. The precise wall gap and cause were not recorded; no clock-adjustment cause is claimed. One shared wait now rechecks actual UnixMilli after each context-bound timer wake for both original daily due and job expiry. It retains the same targets/global900-second deadline, records observed/target milliseconds on failures, and phase06 binds observed expiry/winner wall times.
 
